[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":333},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news:\u002Fnews\u002F2007-02-18-lunar-1-6-1-installer-iso-moose-drool-released-for-i686":3,"news-timeline":114},{"id":4,"title":5,"author":6,"body":7,"date":104,"description":105,"extension":106,"meta":107,"navigation":108,"path":109,"readingTime":110,"seo":111,"stem":112,"__hash__":113},"news\u002Fnews\u002F2007-02-18-lunar-1-6-1-installer-iso-moose-drool-released-for-i686.md","Lunar 1.6.1 installer iso \"Moose Drool\" released for i686 and x86_64","sofar",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":100},"minimark",[10,14,17,20,23,26,29,56,59,82,85,94,97],[11,12,13],"p",{},"Hi,",[11,15,16],{},"With great pleasure we release \"Moose Drool\", also known as the Lunar-Linux 1.6.1 Installer ISO in to the public.",[11,18,19],{},"This ISO is partially a refreshed installer for i686, but it is also our first stable ISO for x86_64. The x86_64 installer ISO thus marks the true final entry for Lunar Linux as a multi-arch distro. This ISO comes with gcc-3.4.6, glibc-2.3.6, linux-2.6.20, perl-5.8.8, and other rock solid base components.",[11,21,22],{},"Allthough the x86_64 ISO is purely 64-bit only now, we're working behind the scenes to enable multilib, so stay focused for more news on that. This will also be the last iso with gcc-3.x. Future ISO's will move to gcc-4.x and an updated glibc. Many more new things are to come!",[11,24,25],{},"Download it here:",[11,27,28],{},"i686: [257MB]",[30,31,32,42,49],"ul",{},[33,34,35],"li",{},[36,37,41],"a",{"href":38,"rel":39},"https:\u002F\u002Fdownload.lunar-linux.org\u002Flunar\u002Flunar-1.6.1-i686.iso.bz2",[40],"nofollow","lunar-1.6.1-i686.iso.bz2",[33,43,44],{},[36,45,48],{"href":46,"rel":47},"https:\u002F\u002Fdownload.lunar-linux.org\u002Flunar\u002Flunar-1.6.1-i686.iso.bz2.md5",[40],"lunar-1.6.1-i686.iso.bz2.md5",[33,50,51],{},[36,52,55],{"href":53,"rel":54},"https:\u002F\u002Fdownload.lunar-linux.org\u002Flunar\u002Flunar-1.6.1-i686.iso.md5",[40],"lunar-1.6.1-i686.iso.md5",[11,57,58],{},"x8